<title>NEW ZEALAND: ANZ cuts NZ variable mortgage rate to 9.4 pct.</title>
<headline>ANZ cuts NZ variable mortgage rate to 9.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANZ Banking Group New Zealand Ltd and its subsidiary PostBank said on Thursday they had cut their New Zealand variable home lending rate to 9.4 percent from 9.95 percent.</p>
<p>The move will be effective for new applications from April 28, and for existing customers from June 4.</p>
<p>The cut was the result of recent falls in short term wholesale market interest rates, spokesman Rob Carthew said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
</text>
